App_konference on FreeBSD
=========================

App_konference can be built and used on FreeBSD with Asterisk 20 LTS
(official port net/asterisk20). No changes to the module source code are
needed.

A ready FreeBSD port, net/asterisk20-appkonference, is available at:

    https://github.com/mambursoft/freebsd-asterisk20-appkonference

It is tested on FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE amd64 with asterisk20-20.22.0 (clang).

Quick start
-----------

    git clone https://github.com/mambursoft/freebsd-asterisk20-appkonference
    cp -R freebsd-asterisk20-appkonference/net/asterisk20-appkonference \
          /usr/ports/net/
    make -C /usr/ports/net/asterisk20-appkonference install clean

Then add to /usr/local/etc/asterisk/modules.conf:

    load => app_konference.so

What the port does with the upstream Makefile
---------------------------------------------

The port adapts the Makefile at build time (post-patch), the source code is
used as is:

  - ASTERISK_SRC_DIR=/usr/local (installed Asterisk headers),
    ASTERISK_SRC_VERSION=2000, INSTALL_MODULES_DIR is set by the port;
  - CPPFLAGS += -DKQUEUE (BSD timing) and -DAC_USE_ALAW (ULAW + ALAW);
  - CFLAGS/CPPFLAGS are appended to (not replaced), so the ports flags are
    kept; the link step uses $(LDFLAGS);
  - -fcommon for GCC 10+ and clang, -std=gnu89;
  - the module is installed with the port's own install step, because the
    upstream "install" target does not use DESTDIR.

Note on chan_sip
----------------

In net/asterisk20 the legacy chan_sip is the "SIP" option and it is off by
default. Enable it when building Asterisk if your dialplan uses SIP/ channels.

